From e9779dadc2968aa3341b999845dc6c6211062abf Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: tbrasselle <tbrasselle@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 18 Nov 2026 18:07:51 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] feat(ui): save and restore panel setups

Add a Panel setups window, opened from the View door's "Panel setups..."
row (#2339). The window saves the dock as it stands under a name, puts a
saved arrangement back, deletes one, toggles auto-load, and reaches the
existing "Reset layout".

- Which panels are open, where each is attached (a split side, or a float
  with its rect) and how (leaf size, tab order, active tab, collapsed) are
  kept as the dock's own egui_dock JSON behind a camcraft-panel-setups/1
  format tag. egui_dock's serde feature is now on and Tab derives serde.
- The setups are application settings in panel-setups.json beside the
  theme, never the project file. Auto-load is on by default; the last
  saved or loaded setup starts the next run.
- A corrupt or older file, or a dock that breaks the permanence law
  (a floating viewport, a rootless main area), loads the default layout
  with a diagnostic. A load is view state: it rides a one-frame mailbox,
  never the command history.
- Unlaid-out rects (infinite, which JSON spells null) are saved as a
  placeholder so a fresh float still reads back.

Tests: save_then_load_restores_the_panel_setup,
the_saved_setup_starts_the_next_run,
auto_load_off_starts_with_the_default_layout,
a_corrupt_setup_loads_the_default_layout_with_a_diagnostic,
an_older_setups_file_starts_the_default_layout,
a_viewport_in_a_float_is_refused, layout_window_panel_setups.

Fixes #2339

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.2 <noreply@anthropic.com>
